# Sample `.spec` File

```spec
Name:           hello
Version:        1.0
Release:        1%{?dist}
Summary:        Simple Hello World program

License:        MIT
Source0:        hello-1.0.tar.gz

BuildRequires:  gcc

%description
A simple hello world program written in C.

%prep
%setup -q

%build
gcc %{optflags} -o hello hello.c

%install
mkdir -p %{buildroot}/usr/bin
install -m 0755 hello %{buildroot}/usr/bin/hello

%check
./hello | grep "Hello"

%files
/usr/bin/hello
%doc README.md
%license LICENSE

%post
echo "Thank you for installing hello!"

%changelog
* Sat Jul 05 2025 Yashwanth Rathakrishnan <you@example.com> - 1.0-1
- Initial package
```

## 1. `%prep` Section
Prepares source code, unpacks files, apply patches, etc.
```spec
%prep
setup -q
```
`setup -q` unpacks the main source tarball (`Source0`) into a directory named `<name>-<version>`.

## 2. `%build` Section
It compile/build the software
```spec
%build
gcc %{optflags} -o hello hello.c
```
`%{optflags}` uses distro-recommended compiler flags for security and compatibility. Ensure that you add this flag when building binaries/executables.

## 3. `%install` Section
Install files into a temporary buildroot.
```sh
%install
mkdir -p %{buildroot}/usr/bin
install -m 0755 hello %{buildroot}/usr/bin/hello
```
`%{buildroot}` is a macro for the temporary install root.

## 4. `%files` Section
List files to include in the final RPM.
```spec
%files
/usr/bin/hello
%doc README.md
%license LICENSE
```
- `/usr/bin/hello` = binary. (_macro_)
- `%doc` = documentation file(s). (_macro_)
- `%license` = indicates the `LICENSE` file(s). (_macro_)

## 5. `%changelog` Section
Track changes for each version, mostly used for tracking the specified changes made on certain versions.
```sh
%changelog
* Sat Jul 05 2025 Yashwanth Rathakrishnan <iamyaash@mail.com> - 1.0-1
- Package initialization
```

## 6. `%check` Section
Runs tests to verify the build.
```spec
%check
./hello | grep "Hello"
```
It just checks the output when `hello` is executed, but checking the package might vary based on the usage.

## 7. Scriptlets
### `%post`
Execute the command(s) **after installing** the package.
```sh
%post
echo "Thank you for install hello-1.0"
```
### `%pre`
Execute the command(s) **before installing** the package.
```sh
%pre
echo "Initiating the package installation..."
```
### `%preun`
Execute the command(s) **after uninstalling/removing** the package.
```sh
%preun
echo "Removed hello pacakge"
```
### `%postun`
Execute the command(s) **before uninstalling/removing** the package.
```sh
%postun
echo "Uninstalling the hello package
```
